94: However, current indexers still score every preceding key, or block of keys, for each query. This remains expensive (quadratic in prefill, linear in decode), and becomes a bottleneck at long context  ( Zan et al., 2026 ; Xu et al., 2026 ) . For example, at 10M tokens, 98% of the prefill time of a sparse attention layer is spent on indexing (Figure  2 ).
