 Table  1 provides an overview of the existing work on sparse attention, as categorised above.
We focus on methods that keep the whole KV cache and select keys per query, unlike fixed sparse patterns  ( Child et al., 2019 ; Beltagy et al., 2020 ; Zaheer et al., 2020 ) and KV cache eviction techniques  ( Zhang et al., 2023b ; Li et al., 2024 ; Xiao et al., 2024b ) . 
 Among distillation methods, DSA  ( DeepSeek-AI, 2025 ) and MiniMax SA  ( Lai et al., 2026 ) first distil the indexer and then continue training the full model under sparse attention.
Alternatively, SeerAttention  ( Gao et al., 2025 ; Gao et al., 2026 ) distils a gate over pooled blocks and HashAttention  ( Desai et al., 2025 ) learns binary codes of queries and keys, both with the model frozen.
As the context grows, the indexer itself becomes the bottleneck  ( Xu et al., 2026 ; Zan et al., 2026 ; Bai et al., 2026 ) .
To reduce its cost, CSA  ( DeepSeek-AI, 2026a ) , QSA  ( Qwen Team, 2026a ) , and GLM-5.3-Flash SA  ( Z.ai, 2026 ) compress every four keys into one before scoring them.
HISA  ( Xu et al., 2026 ) and LongCat LSA  ( Zan et al., 2026 ) score blocks first and then only the keys inside the selected blocks.
IndexCache  ( Bai et al., 2026 ) , LongCat LSA and DeepSeek-V4.1  ( DeepSeek-AI, 2026b ) reuse the selection of one layer in the following layers.
Each improvement divides the cost of the indexer by a constant, and its work per query therefore still grows linearly with the context. 
 NSA  ( Yuan et al., 2025 ) and MoBA  ( Lu et al., 2025 ) instead pre-train the model with sparse attention from scratch, such that the indexer learns from the NTP loss alone.
NSA scores each block by a learned compressed key, and MoBA by the mean of its keys.
InfLLM-V2  ( Zhao et al., 2026 ) and SSA  ( Mao et al., 2026a ) bring such block selection to existing dense models by fine-tuning.
HSA  ( Hu et al., 2025 ; Leng et al., 2026 ; Hu et al., 2026a ) and HSA-UltraLong  ( Hu et al., 2026b ) also weight the output of each block by its score, such that the loss trains the scores directly.
