80:However, at ultra-long context (above 1M tokens), full attention is prohibitively expensive. A promising approach is sparse attention, in which a dedicated indexer selects a subset of keys for the attention. Yet current methods of indexing either still have quadratic cost in context size or lose accuracy at ultra-long context scale.
90:In line with this trend, recent models extend their context windows to 1M tokens and beyond  ( Gemini Team, 2024 ; MiniMax, 2025 ; DeepSeek-AI, 2026a ; Qwen Team, 2026a ) . 
