Table  3 shows that the speedup of one layer carries over to the whole model at ultra-long context.
On GLM-5.3-Flash , D-LSA (Flat) is on par with baseline sparse attention up to 1M tokens with CP8 and already 1.5 × \times faster to first token at 1M with TP8, and at 10M tokens reduces the TTFT by 2.2 × \times and the TPOT by 2.1 × \times with CP8, and by 5.8 × \times and 1.9 × \times with TP8.
On Qwen-3.8-27B , it reduces them by 9.2 × \times and 2.9 × \times at 10M tokens against baseline Full Attention.
On B300, D-LSA (Flat) reduces the TTFT and the TPOT at 10M tokens by 1.6 × \times and 2.2 × \times with CP8 and by 4.8 × \times and 2.6 × \times with TP8 on GLM-5.3-Flash , and by 5.7 × \times and 1.5 × \times on Qwen-3.8-27B .
The speedup of the whole model is expected to be smaller than that of one layer, as only the global attention layers become faster, while the other layers keep their cost. 
